{
  "__comment": "Packet B7-3 / BUGS.md SKB-017: a modulation source wired from the voice domain into the bus domain. The LFO modulates the cutoff of a Filter that sits DOWNSTREAM of the Delay, so it belongs in the bus block. Evaluated per voice (the old behaviour) its output was summed across active voices — depth scaled with how many keys were down — and collapsed to zero the moment the last voice released, which is mid-delay-tail here (mix 1.0, feedback 0.9, note gone by ~0.25s). The acceptance case measures the tail's brightness a half LFO period apart and requires it to still be swinging.",
